Once, a rich man boarded a luxury cruise ship with his wife. The man was extremely
stingy and always tried to save money.
During dinner, he noticed that the prices at the ship's restaurant were ridiculously high.
So, he told his wife,
Husband: "Why should we spend so much on food? Let’s just go back to our cabin and
eat bread and cheese."
The wife reluctantly agreed.
The next day, the ship encountered a severe storm, and everyone was asked to get on
the lifeboats. The stingy husband quickly jumped into a lifeboat, but his wife was still
running toward him.
Husband (shouting): "Hurry up, or the lifeboat will leave without you!"
Wife (panting): "Does it cost anything to get on the lifeboat?"
